Output:
## Examples (MOST IMPORTANT)
- examples/toolkits/arxiv_toolkit.py
  - Shows: Creating a ChatAgent with ArxivToolkit tools
  - Key usage: Searching and downloading papers from arXiv using agent steps

- examples/knowledge_graph/knowledge_graph_agent_example.py
  - Shows: Usage of KnowledgeGraphAgent with UnstructuredIO for text processing
  - Key usage: Running agent with text elements and custom prompts

## Implementation
- camel/toolkits/arxiv_toolkit.py
  - Classes: ArxivToolkit
  - Methods: search_papers, download_papers, get_tools
  - Description: Toolkit for interacting with arXiv API to search and download papers

- camel/retrievers/vector_retriever.py
  - Classes: VectorRetriever
  - Methods: process, query
  - Description: Retriever implementation using vector storage and embedding models for query-based retrieval

- camel/toolkits/function_tool.py
  - Classes: FunctionTool
  - Methods: __init__, __call__, async_call, get_openai_tool_schema, synthesize_openai_tool_schema, etc.
  - Description: Abstraction for functions that OpenAI chat models can call, with schema generation and async support

## Configuration
- camel/configs/base_config.py
  - Classes: BaseConfig
  - Description: Base configuration class for models, including validation for tools (FunctionTool instances)

## Benchmarks (related to RAG and vector retrieval)
- camel/benchmarks/ragbench.py
  - Classes: RAGBenchBenchmark
  - Methods: download, load, run
  - Description: Benchmark for evaluating retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) systems with context relevancy and faithfulness metrics

These files collectively provide the components and usage patterns for creating an agent with Arxiv tools, downloading papers, and performing vector retrieval to answer questions. The example in examples/toolkits/arxiv_toolkit.py is especially relevant as it demonstrates searching and downloading papers with an agent using ArxivToolkit. The vector_retriever.py file shows how vector retrieval is implemented. The function_tool.py file is important for understanding how tools are wrapped for model usage. The ragbench.py benchmark shows usage of retrieval and agent interaction in evaluation scenarios.
